2500 Tree Diagram Ruleset
=========================

Illustrates tree-like architecture or workflow diagram in Unicode characters.


Structure
---------

1. Use [ ] for major components, services, resources, or logical containers.

   ├─ [ Component ]
   ├─ [ Service ]
   └─ [ Database ]

2. Use ├─, └─, and │ to nest child components under parent components
   for hierarchy, ownership, or containment.

   [ Parent Component ]
    ├─ [ Child Component A ]
    └─ [ Child Component B ]

3. Use < > for placeholders, omitted items, repeated patterns, or variable names.

   ├─ Name: < component name >
   ├─ Type: <>
   └─ < other components >

4. Do not bracket small details.

   Brackets are only for major components.

   Good:
   ├─ [ API Service ]
   │   └─ Runtime: container

   Avoid:
   ├─ [ API Service ]
   │   └─ [ Runtime: container ]


Content
-------

5. Use key-value lines for attributes.

   ├─ Key: value

   Examples:
   ├─ Name: gear.go
   ├─ Version: 3.12
   ├─ Type: <>
   └─ Role: <>

6. Use numbered action lines when sequence matters.

   ├─ (1) Action name: optional summary
   ├─ (2) Action name: optional summary
   └─ (3) Action name: optional summary

   Numbers show order, not unique IDs.
   Repeat a number for simultaneous actions.

7. Use bullet lines for action details.

   Place details under the related action.

   ├─ (1) Action name: optional summary
   │     * detail
   │     * detail


Relationships
-------------

8. Use a Links section for relationships between components.

   Place Links under the nearest common parent.

   ├─ Links:
   │  ├─ [ Source Component A ]
   │  │  --> [ Target Component A ]: relationship
   │  │
   │  └─ [ Source Component B ]
   │     <-> [ Target Component B ]: relationship

   Use --> for one-way relationships.
   Use <-> for two-way relationships.

9. Stack target components under common source component in Links.

   ├─ Links:
   │  └─ [ Source Component ]
   │     --> [ Target Componet A ]: relationship
   │     <-> [ Target Componet B ]: relationship


Style
-----

10. Keep one idea per line.

11. Prefer clarity over completeness.

12. Include only details that serve the diagram's purpose.


